    "body": "Oh sorry, `\\` is not applicable then I think. I got this confused with the people who think all inputs ought to be valid or rejected. Whereas you don't necessarily think all inputs ought to be valid or rejected, but the invalid inputs that are accepted, ought to be transformed to something valid when they are spit out again.\r\n\r\nSo yeah, the reason for that is mainly encouraging RFC 3986 interop. But I'm not sure anyone is really appreciative of that.",
